Optimize this fixed combinational instance: module addr_calcu, parameters {"base": 128}. Minimize mapped maximum data arrival. Give one complete synthesizable Verilog-2001 design. Keep module, parameters, ports, widths, signedness, truncations, priority and default-case behavior. All inputs are unconstrained, all outputs must match for every two-state input. No clocks, storage, latency, assumptions, external includes, or new dependencies. Helper modules are allowed.
Common evaluation: SKY130HD TT25C1.80V; zero external IO delays; input transition0.10ns; output load0.010pF; 100ns virtual reporting clock; no physical wire parasitics. Yosys flatten/synth-noabc; ABC strash/dretime/map/cleanup-i-o/buffer/upsize/dnsize/stime-p with fixed driver and load. Full source and mapped equivalence and zero electrical violations required.
Baseline mapped area 1192.393600um^2; fixed cap 1311.632960um^2. No candidate results are supplied.
Return exactly one JSON object with these six fields: candidate_rtl, bottleneck, rewrite, expected_timing_gain, area_or_other_cost, functional_boundaries.
Original RTL:
module addr_calcu(
    input [7:0] address,
    input [7:0] ptr1, ptr2,
    input [7:0] b,
    input control, // control is late arriving
    output [15:0] count
);

    parameter [7:0] base = 8'b10000000;

    wire [7:0] offset1, offset2;
    wire [15:0] addr1, addr2;
    wire [15:0] count1, count2;

    assign offset1 = base - ptr1;
    assign offset2 = base - ptr2;
    assign addr1 = address - {8'h00, offset1};
    assign addr2 = address - {8'h00, offset2};
    assign count1 = addr1 + b;
    assign count2 = addr2 + b;
    assign count = (control == 1'b1) ? count1 : count2;

endmodule
